 # Flight Logbook
 
 > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.
 > Newest entries first. One block per insight.
 
 ## 2026-08-30
 
 ### 0331 — Advisory samples are fresh evidence inside one serialized watermark controller (TASK-260715-3kjhkw)
 
 - IMPLEMENTATION: `MemoryWatermarkController` combines a new platform sample with timestamped ledger current/reserved/committed/peak bytes on one actor. iOS calls `os_proc_available_memory()` for every accepted observation; macOS reports the public API as unsupported instead of substituting host memory. Physical footprint and peak use `TASK_VM_INFO` on both platforms.
 - STATE: Inclusive Soft/Pressure/Critical entry takes the maximum of ledger headroom, configured-baseline physical headroom, advisory bytes, and memory warning. Recovery is strict-above the configured exit floor, requires fresh available evidence plus action acknowledgement and dwell, and moves at most one state per evaluation. Per-trigger event limiting prevents ordinary events from suppressing a simultaneous warning.
 - REVIEW REWORK: A reviewer negative test proved that a fresh warning could previously lower Pressure to Soft when the byte signals permitted recovery. `nextState` now clamps one-step recovery to the strongest entry signal in the same observation; a warning permits Critical to recover only to Pressure and cannot recover below Pressure. The committed regression test covers both boundaries.
 - BOUNDS/PRIVACY: Cadence, per-trigger event interval, evidence age, sampling-duration classification, history capacity (maximum 1,024), sequence, and fixed enum cardinality are explicit. Malformed, stale, unavailable, overflowed, or late evidence cannot recover state. Metrics and observations accept no destination, host, payload, credential, or free-form label.
 - REWORK: Self-review rejected a zero event interval, thresholds outside their finite ledger/physical ranges, and a ledger peak below committed bytes. The first tightened focused run then failed because cadence was measured finish-to-start and coalesced callers after one full-budget sample; production now measures start-to-start, so sampling work itself consumes the interval without allowing an unbounded zero interval.
 - VERIFICATION: Twelve deterministic Swift Testing cases cover real platform sampling, threshold equality/one-over, jumps, hysteresis, stale/unavailable evidence, warning bursts, action acknowledgement, configuration replacement, 64 concurrent observations, checked overflow, history, cardinality, and recovery. The final 256-sample macOS probe measured 0.000319625 seconds total and 0.000012042 seconds maximum. Generic iOS Simulator `ReluxTunnelCore` build succeeded; recursive Swift format passed; `make validate-core` passed 518 tests in 43 suites plus the post-test build, with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues.
 - BOARD ANOMALY: Both board validations exited 0 but reported `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for this Story and unrelated `STORY-260715-1y04r0`. The developer handoff correctly moved this task to `to-review` but the parent remained `to-dev` instead of its computed `to-review`; the specialist did not overwrite parent lifecycle state.
 
 ### 0315 — Receive-window credit is bounded by one value-semantic ledger (TASK-260715-3kimon)
 
 - IMPLEMENTATION: Core selects control, ordinary, capped-BDP bulk, and relay control-plus-UDP-burst initial windows with checked configuration and saturating arithmetic. Initial and earned adjustment credit reserve per-channel, per-lane, global-window, and global-ledger capacity before admission; releases are exact and idempotent.
 - GATES: Soft caps only new initial windows. Pressure withholds every adjustment and nonessential opens; Critical, rekeying, failed, closing, closed, stale-generation, low-water, and insufficient-reservation paths refuse without changing or queueing credit. Previously advertised credit is never represented as revoked.
 - ADAPTER: Both libssh2 `libssh2_channel_open_ex` call sites use one tested initial-window conversion. The adapter still truthfully reports consumer-driven adjustment as unsupported; no protocol message is sent outside that adapter.
-- VERIFICATION: Eleven policy tests cover tables, 32/64 KiB, capped and overflowing BDP, relay bursts, all budget ceilings, pressure/lane/generation gates, exact lifecycle reconciliation, and 2,000 deterministic randomized transitions. One selected-adapter test covers all four classes. The full 506-test Swift suite passed with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues; recursive Swift format, core boundaries, diff check, and `swift build` exited 0.
+- REVIEW REWORK: Revision-1 review found that `reserveAdjustment` treated reserved capacity as one-shot credit and retained an unbounded UUID tombstone set. Adjustment now separates reusable capacity from `newlyReservedBytes`, repeatedly restores outstanding credit to the immutable cap without growing lane/global/ledger totals, rejects impossible outstanding-credit reports, and makes absent release an idempotent zero-release without retaining channel identity.
+- VERIFICATION: Twelve policy tests cover tables, 32/64 KiB, capped and overflowing BDP, relay bursts, all budget ceilings, pressure/lane/generation gates, exact lifecycle reconciliation, four repeated replenishments, 10,000 unknown/released-channel churn cycles, and 2,000 deterministic randomized transitions. One selected-adapter test covers all four classes. The full 519-test Swift suite passed with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues; strict recursive Swift format, core boundaries, diff check, and `swift build` exited 0.
 
 ### Cross-layer memory authority separates reservation from physical evidence (TASK-260715-1pn983)
 
 - DECISION: One checked-byte ledger owns packet, HEV, SSH, DNS, client relay, rekey, metrics, and reconnect admissions. SSH credit is separate from resident bytes but reserves permitted local storage; failed reads are unknown, never zero or absence.
 - REVIEW REWORK: Revision-1 review found that the untracked reserve could be spent, total and incremental reservations were conflated, lane admission had no closed predicate, the reconnect/KEX view appeared to drop a permanent reserve, and the packet-plane target still named the deferred iPhone. Revision 2 makes `B_untracked` a permanent charged row, uses total-capacity rows plus candidate deltas, defines atomic lane admission and exact failed-construction release, separates reconnect from permanent KEX state, and aligns the active target to the named physical Apple-silicon Mac.
 - DNS RESIDUAL: The hard candidate ledger is 7,635,554 bytes inside an 8,388,608-byte component budget. Combined with the accepted 9,715,712-byte incremental HEV/bridge peak, it leaves 8,110,080 bytes in the lower 25 MiB engineering envelope. This proves arithmetic fit only; production remains false pending complete physical composition.
 - PRESSURE: Deterministic Soft/Pressure/Critical entry, hysteretic one-level recovery, one ordered action table, KEX emergency reservation, atomic replacement reservation, old-transport-first Critical release, and explicit stop replace jetsam-driven or side-queue behavior.
 - GAPS: Final watermarks, BDP/window winners, component ceilings, untracked reserve, overlap, and iPhone rows remain evidence-gated. No Apple guarantee, payload capture, flow migration, or weakened gate is asserted.
 
 ### M0 packet bridge and HEV baseline accepted (TASK-260715-2jatnd)
 
 - DECISION: The macOS-first M0 Bridge gate passes under ADR-024 with MTU 1500, requested/effective 32768-byte socket buffers, 64-packet/5-ms pump budgets, HEV task-stack/TCP/UDP-copy values 24576/4096/2, and an initial measured 500-session ceiling. MTU 4096 remains injectable behind end-to-end proof; MTU 8500 is a named failed default candidate because constrained-buffer rows produced 768 `EMSGSIZE` refusals.
 - EVIDENCE: Public-API bridge, IPv4/IPv6 framing, deterministic faults, hostile-frame fuzzing, bounded pressure, lifecycle, packaging, notices, and physical Mac MTU/memory rows trace to accepted task-scoped resources in `docs/TASK-260715-2jatnd_m0-bridge-hev-decision-adr.md`. The worst measured incremental HEV/bridge cost was 9,715,712 bytes at 500 sessions; whole-extension SSH/DNS/relay/cache/reconnect memory remains unmeasured.
 - FORK: Unmodified HEV `ad7600497931205105b08367bd1b450048157e40` remains selected. There is no Instruments material-bottleneck evidence or improved callback prototype, so fork authorization is rejected by default.
 - GAPS: Physical iPhone, jetsam, NAT64, sleep/wake, energy, and whole-extension memory stay deferred/blocked and are never inferred from macOS. M1 consumers may use this baseline only through the exact accepted-outcome binding task; production composition remains fail-closed on its other M0 inputs.
 
 ## 2026-08-27
 
 ### 0824 — Deterministic lifecycle release is separated from Darwin residency (TASK-260715-135rr8)
 - ROOT CAUSE: The rev3 gate coupled two distinct claims. Harness-owned channels, reads, queues, boundary/native lifecycle counters, and descriptor-close stages were released deterministically, but the gate still required Darwin to return allocator pages during the same 500-cycle observation. One reviewer run therefore failed on a bounded `+180224 B` non-decreasing footprint rise while the next two passed.
 - FIX: The schema-2 lifecycle evidence now records an `ownedResourcesReleased` verdict and every underlying ownership field for each cycle. The production gate requires 500 cycles, zero failed owned-resource-release cycles, and the unchanged post-warmup maximum resident-footprint drawup ceiling of `256 KiB`. Monotonic and late rises remain classified with exact transition/cycle evidence, but OS page-return timing is no longer used as a proxy for product-owned release. The matrix atomically emits its exact-tree-bound raw report before returning a failing verdict.
 - NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: Production-call-site tests reject 499 cycles, a footprint overflow, and one missing owned-resource release at cycle 499. A separate emission-order test proves the raw-evidence closure runs before the production gate throws. Forged working-tree and HEV artifact provenance remain fail-closed.
 - EXPLORATORY MEASUREMENT: A fresh exact-tree 500-cycle loopback probe reproduced the allocator ambiguity with `+147480 B` net change and `180248 B` maximum drawup while all `500/500` cycles restored every owned resource. Descriptors returned from 9 to 3, threads from 9 to 7, and the deterministic release gate passed. This supports signal separation without widening the 500-cycle or 256 KiB bounds.
 
 ### 0751 — Lifecycle observer allocation removed before classification (TASK-260715-135rr8)
 - ROOT CAUSE/FIX: `measureRealHEVLifecycle` retained every sample in an initially empty Swift `Array` after taking its baseline. The observer now reserves the exact bounded cycle count before the baseline snapshot. A production-call-site regression asserts capacity for 1000 samples, and the diagnostic entry accepts only 100/500/1000 cycles; malformed or wider values fail closed.
 - MEASUREMENT: Corrected exact-tree loopback probes ran 100/500/1000 real HEV cycles. Post-warmup net change was `+81,944 B` / `-212,992 B` / `-32,768 B`; maximum drawup was `98,328 B` / `65,536 B` / `65,536 B`; increase/equal/decrease transitions were `3/85/1`, `4/479/6`, and `7/977/5`. The prior late approximately 16 KiB jumps above cycle 1000 disappeared; the last 1000-cycle increase was cycle 481. Every sample restored live sessions, reads, and queues to zero; descriptors ended at 3 and threads at 8.
 - RULE: A fresh production-entry repeat proved 100 cycles insufficient: it stopped fail-closed on one `+65,536 B` increase and no release. The simplest repeatable gate therefore uses the next predeclared row, 500 cycles, after fixed 10-sample warmup. It permits a full plateau or a measured release only while maximum drawup stays within 256 KiB (1% of the upper 25 MiB target); late unreleased rise and a released-but-over-ceiling linear sawtooth fail closed. The earlier 2000-cycle/trailing-1000 rule measured observer allocation and is retired rather than widened further.
 
 ### 0732 — Extended lifecycle converges to a bounded HEV/runtime envelope (TASK-260715-135rr8)
 - INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
 - RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 2000 samples (20× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, post-warmup and trailing 1000-sample maximum drawup no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope), and either a trailing plateau or an observed post-warmup release. Maximum drawup measures each upward excursion from the running minimum, so a large release is not itself a failure. Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive plateau and bounded-oscillation tests plus unreleased late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
